{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the Tent of Meeting shall set out.</b> After these two standards." "<b>As they encamp, so shall they set out.</b> As I have explained — their marching is like their encamping: each standard marches in the direction fixed for it." "<b>עַל יָדוֹ.</b> At its place — and the term יָד does not depart from its meaning: the side-direction of its flank is called עַל יָדוֹ, [meaning] what is adjacent to it for the full reach of its hand; אינשו\"ן איש\"א בְּלַעַ\"ז."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "the la'az appears to be Old French en son iśiśa — 'at its side/location'; the reading is uncertain and the phrase is textually obscure."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:11.777781079Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}